        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: Through a Glass Window, I Loved a Soldier\n- People: Maurice Campbell, Olga Printzlau, Henry Hathaway\n- Companies: Paramount Pictures, Viacom\n- Places: Hollywood, California\n\nFacts:\n- Through a Glass Window is a 1922 American drama silent film.\n- Through a Glass Window was directed by Maurice Campbell and written by Olga Printzlau.\n- Paramount Pictures Corporation is an American film studio based in Hollywood, California.\n- Paramount Pictures has been a subsidiary of Viacom since 1994.\n- I Loved a Soldier, also known as Invitation to Happiness, is an unfinished 1936 American romantic-comedy-drama film.\n- I Loved a Soldier was directed by Henry Hathaway and produced by Paramount Pictures.",
